  "claim": "In 1957 the Britain Burma Society was founded under the distinguished patronage of Earl Mountbatten of Burma, Sir Hubert Rance, whose formal prefix Sir was strictly governed by law and custom as an honorific address.",
  "evidencia": "Page: Britain–Burma Society. Sentence: The Britain Burma Society (BBS) is a society founded in 1957 under the distinguished patronage of Earl Mountbatten of Burma, Sir Hubert Rance (formerly Governor of Burma), Miss Dorothy Woodman, the Rt.\nPage: Sir. Sentence: Sir is an honorific address used in a number of situations in many anglophone cultures.\nPage: Sir. Sentence: The term can be used as a formal prefix, especially in the Commonwealth, for males who have been given certain honours or titles (such as knights and baronets), where usage is strictly governed by law and custom.",
