        "original_id": "68825422-e1a9-533a-8f4b-ac4fa04f7e7f",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Organizations: Britain Burma Society\n- People: Earl Mountbatten of Burma, Sir Hubert Rance, Dorothy Woodman\n- Titles: Sir\n- Places: Burma, Commonwealth\n\nFacts:\n- In 1957, the Britain Burma Society was founded under the patronage of Earl Mountbatten of Burma, Sir Hubert Rance, and Dorothy Woodman.\n- Sir Hubert Rance was formerly Governor of Burma.\n- Sir is an honorific form of address used in many anglophone cultures.\n- In the Commonwealth, Sir can be used as a formal prefix for males who have received certain honours or titles, such as knighthoods and baronetcies, and its use is governed by law and custom.",
